// Regression: two imported modules exporting a same-named `pub fn` of DIFFERENT
// arity must not corrupt one module's own unqualified internal call.
//
// a.handle(string) and b.handle() share the name; module a calls its own handle
// unqualified. Before the fix, codegen emitted `handle_string(s)` inside a's
// use_it - an overload-mangled callee that nothing defines, since a module pub fn
// is emitted as `<mod>_handle`. The build died with "call to undeclared function
// 'handle_string'" pointing at a line the programmer never wrote, and swapping the
// import order changed whether it compiled. See OPEN-12 in the dogfood findings.
//
// The fix: an unqualified call resolving to a function of the CURRENT module is
// emitted by that module's own C name, never the overload-mangled one, even when
// another imported module has a same-named namesake. Genuine SAME-module
// overloading is unaffected (it resolves within one module and keeps its mangled
// names).
// EXPECT: 5
// EXPECT: 42
import overload_collision_mod
import overload_collision_mod2

fn main() {
    println(overload_collision_mod.use_it("hello"))
    println(overload_collision_mod2.handle())
}
